# Dynamic Recursives

<iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/1UIPcUJwv_g?start=414&end=441" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen></iframe>

[Dynamic Recursion](https://youtu.be/1UIPcUJwv_g?t=414)

> A recursive algorithm is dynamic if there exists some element or elements that change during execution while still maintaining the correct solution.

Source: [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1UIPcUJwv_g&t=414s)

The [algorithmic thinking video series](https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLDkYzPVGzgFQVZAqfKktuLjqxjTzZpE-I) also contains a lecture on dynamic recursion.

---

<a name="example"></a>
## Example

### Problem Statement

Given an array of integers and a target sum `S`, find all pairs of numbers in the given array whose sum equals to the target sum `S`.
